msgid "DroneCAN Servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:7
#: 14f5f8e29cee4b36a3ca9bf17217bcaf
msgid "ArduPilot supports :ref:`DroneCAN<common-uavcan-setup-advanced>` servos. DroneCAN connected servos offer high noise immunity and longer lead runs that normal :ref:`PWM servos<common-servo>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:9
#: 3517fb9acb39492cbf946c549491e52c
msgid "`Currawong <https://www.currawongeng.com/can-servo/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:10
#: 1d28a5db51e248a4a5de10b8db0cfc56
msgid "`Himark <http://himarkuaveng.com/cate-21898-23052.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:11
#: 2f5c495817814095b3a28f38919d5112
msgid "`Hitec <https://www.hiteccs.com/actuators/products/search/servo/1/spec/1-18/accessory/0/sort/0>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:12
#: 6026b7f75d484d55bd45f210232dc123
msgid "`Zeus <http://zeus-actuators.com/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:15
#: a0a3d1b8864c4f53992357603fd0b179
msgid "Autopilot Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:17
#: 4e0de216f736405a80c65e9395dd04e1
msgid "There are several parameters that determine which autopilot servo/motor channels are sent to the DroneCAN servos: For the examples below, the values are shown for DroneCAN driver #1 using CAN Port #1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:20
#: 25ee9e2b2be34cf3815ff4cbc57194d6
msgid ":ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER<CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1, which assigns driver1 to port1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:21
#: fdf88f642362410591e1d09e07ae442e
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL<CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (DroneCAN protocol)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:22
#: 37442903c2234daabca9c00e410a9cdd
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_UC_NODE<CAN_D1_UC_NODE>`: node ID of the autopilot sending the commands to the servos so that there can be differentiation between multiple sources on the CAN bus. This is normally automatically set during discovery, but can be altered for advanced configurations (multiple sources on the bus)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:23
#: 8e56c736aca346369825b308b3664b0d
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_UC_SRV_BM<CAN_D1_UC_SRV_BM>`: bitmask of servo output channels that should be sent via DroneCAN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:24
#: 40919e66878d4d8999e31aebc23a69c7
msgid "(Optionally) :ref:`CAN_D1_UC_SRV_RT<CAN_D1_UC_SRV_RT>`: rate that servo outputs are sent from the autopilot to the actuator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:26
#: 10856e7fb661484a9c96a931c7a6a127
msgid "Himark servos use a different command set. In order to use them, also set :ref:`CAN_D1_UC_OPTION<CAN_D1_UC_OPTION>` bit 5 (+32)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:29
#: abfd98b714de4293bc47db13f54a7bf3
msgid "AP_Periph Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:31
#: b98b40cba2b245db8317fd1f0b587390
msgid "To set up servo control on an AP_Periph node, set the following parameters on the node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:33
#: c99405f89eda408b89d23a6149bff16a
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_FUNCTION<dev:OUT1_FUNCTION>` = 51 for actuator id 1, 52 for actuator id 2, etc. This assigns the output channel to respond to ``uavcan.equipment.actuator.Command``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:34
#: 5864b7619a2c418a8825891a2b80fcdc
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_MIN<dev:OUT1_MIN>` = 1100, the minimum PWM output in microseconds. Set according to servo specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:35
#: 3f6d80694a45487ea0395b3561f38376
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_MAX<dev:OUT1_MAX>` = 1900, the maximum PWM output in microseconds. Set according to servo specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:36
#: 682b2e0b379546548b1212109f964416
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_TRIM<dev:OUT1_TRIM>` = 1500, the PWM output in microseconds at neutral autopilot command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:37
#: 8100f9279a2e461bb63f5f715f4a8df6
msgid ":ref:`OUTx_REVERSED<dev:OUT1_REVERSED>` = 0 (default), set to 1 to reverse the servo direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:38
#: 00fc12134ea140c58de2fb8c6b9ce133
msgid ":ref:`OUT_RATE<dev:OUT_RATE>` = 50 (default), output rate in Hz for all servo outputs on the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:41
#: d6ebaad740b544f2ba099bce5668726d
msgid "Actuator Telemetry Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:43
#: d73d045b198d41b6bda9daf374cf07be
msgid "Some AP_Periph nodes, such as the `Vimdrones L431 CAN Servo Hub <https://dev.vimdrones.com/products/vimdrones_can_servo_hub/>`__, support actuator telemetry via the ``uavcan.equipment.actuator.Status`` message, which allows monitoring of servo current draw and load as a percentage of rated current. Set the following parameters on the node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:45
#: 24294e070b934dd3ab83b4ee4d4868e8
msgid ":ref:`ACT_NUM_CHANS<dev:ACT_NUM_CHANS>` = 4, number of servo channels to monitor for telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:46
#: 123eeef1370344da8f8fe53b26bbf48d
msgid ":ref:`ACT_CURR_PIN1<dev:ACT_CURR_PIN1>` = 9, starting ADC pin for current monitoring on the Vimdrones L431 CAN Servo Hub used in this example. Subsequent channels use the next pins (10, 11, ...) on that node; other AP_Periph hardware may use different ADC pin numbering, so consult the specific AP_Periph board documentation to determine the correct ADC pin IDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:47
#: 8b62cef9ba8b4a88afc3dcb4f5e925db
msgid ":ref:`ACT_AMP_OFFSET<dev:ACT_AMP_OFFSET>` = 0, current sensor offset in mA. Used to zero-calibrate the sensor under no load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:48
#: ca552debe7cd4c9e90b0e0e0236c727e
msgid ":ref:`ACT_AMP_PERVLT<dev:ACT_AMP_PERVLT>` = 100, current sensor scale in mA per volt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:49
#: 7f0bc1e45bb143a6ac498d2e576e3555
msgid ":ref:`ACT_CURR_MAX<dev:ACT_CURR_MAX>` = 2.5, maximum current in Amps, used to calculate ``power_rating_pct`` in the telemetry message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-dronecan-servos.rst:50
#: 680e19e8ad1c4bdb913de1c146578bcd
msgid ":ref:`SRV_TLM_MSG_RATE<dev:SRV_TLM_MSG_RATE>` = 10, rate in Hz at which telemetry messages are sent."
msgstr ""
